tment 5, newcomer -> premium 195 G (both surcharges)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4, newcomer -> premium 115 G (no high-ench surcharge)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword, customer with exactly 2 years -> premium 95 G (loyalty discount applies)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runScenario - quote sequencing\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"second quote in scenario gets 15% follow-up discount -> [49, 43]\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runScenario - claims\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"standard sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400, remainingCap 1600\");\n  it.todo(\"rune damage 200 -> payout 100, remainingCap 400\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench clause then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses, 50% wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full reimbursement)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench only)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword 500 and amulet 300 -> payout 600 (deductible per event)\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword, damage 2500 -> payout 2000 (cap based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"two successive claims of 1500 on a sword -> [1400/rem600, 600/rem0] (cap exhaustion)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords both damaged 500 each -> payout 800, remainingCap 3200\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runScenario - errors\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"unknown item type in quote -> throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references unknown item type -> throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage with negative amount -> throws\");\n  it.todo(\"more damage entries of a type than covered -> throws\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"CLI integration\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"schema example: amulet quote + claim -> [{premium:59},{payout:100,remainingCap:1100}]\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero on unknown item type, writes stderr, no stdout results\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero on negative damage amount\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907120688},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me run the tests first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019PBK6n8P6ATRNf1aDQoR4q","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2516,"output":139,"cacheRead":9692,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12347,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907120688,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-72168f33-2c58-4856-bbfb-6ab14797a099","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_019PBK6n8P6ATRNf1aDQoR4q","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (43 tests | 38 skipped) 2ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed | 38 todo (43)\n   Start at  15:32:04\n   Duration  156ms (transform 26ms, setup 1ms, collect 22ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms, prepare 43ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907124215},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the tests are passing, so now I'm looking at how the `basePremium` function was refactored to see what's being tested.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 5 tests pass. Now let me evaluate the refactoring.\n\n## Refactoring Evaluation\n\n**Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)**:\n- `basePremium(items)` — takes a list of ite