asoning":0,"totalTokens":42595,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907365346,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ecc69ebf-1580-49f8-b36b-13e7e781dd7b","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01XoKuTQGJZmpnGHAVwDtLpZ","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 10 tests still green.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Naming Evaluation (first priority):**\n- `basePremium`, `sumBasePremiums` — both already reveal intent. Kept.\n- The component block-pricing concept was **unnamed inline logic** → extracted to `componentPremium`.\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Extracted `componentPremium(components)` from `basePremium`. Now `basePremium` reads as a one-line composition — `sumBasePremiums(mainItems) + componentPremium(components)` — making the two pricing pathways (flat main items vs. block-priced components) explicit and self-documenting.\n- **Rules 3 & 4:** No duplication found; extraction adds one function boundary but Rule 2 (clarity) outranks Rule 4 (fewest elements) here.\n\n**APP Mass:**\n- `basePremium` body dropped from ~87 to ~15 (two filters + one invocation + one addition), with the ~70-mass grouping/pricing loops relocated into the well-named `componentPremium`. Total mass roughly unchanged (~same components, one added invocation +2), but the mass is now distributed under intention-revealing names rather than concentrated in one dense function.\n\n**Rule 1 (Tests):** All 10 tests passing before and after.\n\n**Mass Change:** basePremium ~87 → ~15 (logic relocated); overall ≈ +2 (single new invocation), justified by the clarity gain per Rule 2 > APP."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent changes: basePremium now groups components by type via a Map; each type of exactly 3 gets BLOCK_PREMIUM=60, otherwise count*unit price.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent changes: basePremium now groups components by type via a Map; each type of exactly 3 gets BLOCK_PREMIUM=60, otherwise count*unit price.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784907368999},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JT3AnNGtnz4SgUbjVyTycS","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Qf6EPNmyQP8TdhrtYVVCVj","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":205,"output":121,"cacheRead":9692,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10018,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907369020,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ef7e8188-dad0-4224-b965-549118b1d2d7","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JT3AnNGtnz4SgUbjVyTycS","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO Claim Office - implementation (stubs; filled in during Green phases)\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  // Main items\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  // Components\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((total, item) => total + BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type], 0);\n}\n\nexport function basePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const components = items.filter((item) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type));\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type));\n\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of components) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  let componentTotal = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countsByType) {\n    componentTotal +=\n      count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n  }\n\n  return sumBasePremiums(mainItems) + componentTotal;\n}\n\nexport function insuranceSum(_items: Item[]): number {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n}\n\nexport function quotePremium(\n  _items: Item[],\n  _yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  _isFollowUp: boolean,\n): number {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n}\n\nexport function roundPremium(_amount: number): number {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n}\n\nexport function roundPayout(_amount: number): number {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n}\n\nexport function runScenario(_scenario: unknown): { results: unknown[] } {\n  return undefined as unknown as { results: unknown[] };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907371044},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Qf6EPNmyQP8TdhrtYVVCVj","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  basePremium,\n  insuranceSum,\n  quotePremium,\n  roundPremium,\n  roundPayout,\n  runScenario,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"basePremium - main item values\", () => {\n  it(\"sword base premium is 100 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"sword\" }])).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"amulet base premium is 60 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"amulet\" }])).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"staff base premium is 80 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"staff\" }])).toBe(80);\n  });\n  it(\"potion base premium is 40 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"potion\" }])).toBe(40);\n  });\n  it(\"single component (rune) base premium is 25 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(25);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"basePremium - building block of 3 alike components\", () => {\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }]),\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block, requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      basePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ]),\n    ).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium(Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }))).toBe(175);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }]),\n    ).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G (two separate blocks)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"insuranceSum\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + 3 runes -> insurance sum 1750 G (block does not affect sum)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"rounding in the MHPCO's favor\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"roundPremium(197.5) -> 198 (rounded up)