turn type is unclear.\n- Rule 3/4: No duplication; can reduce elements by removing the mutable counter.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate Initial APP Mass (runScenario body)**\n\n```\nconst { customer, steps } = scenario;        bindings: customer, steps = 2\nlet quoteCount = 0;                           binding quoteCount 1 + const 0 (1) + assignment 6 = 8\nsteps.map((step) => {...})                    invocation map (2), binding step (1), loop map (5) = 8\n  const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;          binding isFollowUp (1), binding quoteCount (1), const 0 (1), invocation > (2) = 5\n  quoteCount += 1;                            binding quoteCount (1), const 1 (1), assignment (6) = 8\n  premium: quotePremium(...)                  invocation (2), bindings step.items/customer.yearsWithMHPCO/isFollowUp ~ (3) = 5\nreturn { results };                           binding results (1)\n```\nApprox Total Mass: ~37 (dominated by two assignments = 12 and the extra `quoteCount` bindings).\n\nRefactor: use the `map` index (`index > 0`) instead of a mutable counter. This eliminates `let quoteCount = 0` (assignment 6) and `quoteCount += 1` (assignment 6), plus their bindings. Also give the return a proper type."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01W2VnzVgJ34yd3WqmSbB5BR","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: unknown[] } {\n  const { customer, steps } = scenario;\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n\n  const results = steps.map((step) => {\n    const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n    quoteCount += 1;\n    return {\n      premium: quotePremium(step.items, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp),\n    };\n  });\n\n  return { results };\n}","newText":"interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: QuoteResult[] } {\n  const { custom